.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Grotthuss-Draper law: only absorbed light drives photochemistry</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/photochem/quantum_yield/plot_01_grotthuss_draper_absorbed_light`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="The law of photochemical equivalence (Stark 1908, Einstein 1912-1913) says each absorbed quantum activates exactly one molecule. The quantum yield \Phi (moles product / moles photons absorbed), computed by photochemical_quantum_yield, then equals 1 for an ideal one-photon, one-molecule reaction and is less than 1 when the excited molecule has other ways to lose its energy.">

